      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The order is twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO BID with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals:** 1,500 mg/day.\n- **Another dose:** For example, 170 mg or 1,700 mg/day total may have been intended.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg TID, tell me and add a clinical rationale. I can enter it with a note, but I'd suggest pharmacy review first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
